<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  The hints (Table/Hints.h, MahjongHintsComponent). The component answers the row HintsRow of the page Options (MahjongSetHints) and the
  button HintButton (MahjongHintAdvice; it is in the node HintsButton and in ActionsCompact), fills the canvas below and
  draws the marks over the viewer's hand; it comes after the table (layer 5: it reads the layout the table drew) and before the
  canvas so that the variables are set when the canvas draws.
  The canvas lies on the view of the table (SceneView). Its two elements fill free regions that config/TableLayout.xml gives each shape
  (Table/TableRegions.h), clear of the node CenterPanel inside the wall ring, which the hints leave free, and of the plates (MahjongHintsTest
  checks the rectangles against the worst-case layout, the plates and the panel). Where they lie in the landscape, portrait, narrow and
  wide table is the file's, so there is no variant. A region wins over the safe area: the table is a fixed design that the safe area does not
  move, so the elements stay where they are on a screen with a notch or side insets, like the tiles.
  WaitPanel (region table.waiting) is the waiting row, a scrim plate: the caption (24, font 18) and a cell per tile that the viewer's hand
  waits for (WaitCell0..12, 24 x 56: the tile as a UIImage of 24 x 32 whose sprite Tile_<notation> the component sets, and under it the
  count of the copies the viewer cannot see, {hintCountN}, 24 high, font 18). The cells keep their size (13 of them are 312 wide) and the
  caption is as wide as the plate. The caption, the counts and the sentence are AutoFit: at 18 they fill their lines in a window of 1280 x 720
  and shrink in the smallest windows, where a line of 18 units is taller than the 24 the row has. AdviceText (region table.advice, a scrim
  plate) holds the sentence {hintAdvice} of the advice, right of the place of the button HintButton (region table.hintButton), which is
  in the node HintsButton and not here: nothing on this canvas takes input, so it needs no touch size. All start hidden; the component
  shows the panel and the first N cells exactly while hints apply (MahjongGame::HintsOn(), a person at the table, no cover, no Setup, the
  hand being played) and the hand waits, the button while hints apply and the viewer has actions to choose from, and the label while an
  advice is up in the mode Hints (in Coach the sentence is the title of the card CoachCard, node HintsWhy).
-->
<node name="Hints" layer="5" contentVersion="3">
  <components>
    <component type="MahjongHintsComponent" />
    <component type="UICanvasComponent" space="SceneView">
      <elements>
        <element type="UIStack" name="WaitPanel" region="table.waiting" anchor="Stretch" visible="false" direction="Vertical" spacing="0" padding="0" crossAlign="Center" color="0,0,0,200">
